well the former chancellor sunak remains  the front-runner among fellow  conservative mps and one of those who's  throwing their weight behind him is  claire coutinho mr thanks so much for  joining us this morning um so how do you  think he did  i thought he did very well to be honest  i mean he had one of the hardest  messages that he was saying to people he  wanted to be very honest about what was  happening in the economy uh but really i  think that rishi cenak was the person  who looked like he was the one who could  be prime minister in a few weeks he had  an incredibly impressive command of the  detail he also i thought had a clear  plan for the future and particularly to  deal with inflation which i think is our  number one problem at the moment and  most importantly i think he was the one  who wanted to be honest with people and  say these are the challenges are ahead  and this is what we need to do to fix  them  why couldn't he answer the question it  was a yes or no question about boris  johnson's honesty well i think he did  answer that question he said that when  he resigned honesty and trust was part  of that um and i think you know the  truth is that for all mps we will feel  that you know boris johnson for a lot of  people was the person who delivered  brexit i think for a lot of people in  the country that was a  ability to deliver something that was  part of their connection to him and  obviously in the last few months there  have been  other challenges and things which have  happened which meant have meant other  people have felt that he he's not honest  so it's not i think very easy to have  black and white answers to these um  questions but the truth is a number of  people resigned from government last  week and rishi net was one of them but  he couldn't say boris johnson was honest  so do you think  he's honest  about that and  why couldn't he just say no to that  question if that's what he thinks well i  think he was very honest about that he  